    dict(key='01-poster', kind='poster', title='Digital Signatures with Bouncy Castle and OpenSSL',
         body=None,
         narration="Hello, and welcome. [[slnc 400]] This video explains digital signatures with Bouncy Castle and OpenSSL, in Java. [[slnc 300]] This video is presented by Jayasekhar Konduru. [[slnc 600]] A digital signature proves that a message was signed with one private key, and not changed afterwards. [[slnc 300]] Anyone with the matching public key can check it. [[slnc 500]] Like a notary's stamp: it proves the stamp was used on this paper, not who the notary really is. [[slnc 600]] The domain is an online bank. [[slnc 400]] You will see how an E C D S A signature, short for Elliptic Curve Digital Signature Algorithm, is made, number by number. [[slnc 300]] The one mistake that gives the key away. [[slnc 300]] And what a valid signature still does not tell you."),
