    dict(key='16-act-4-figure', kind='figure', title='How a JWS token is built',
         body='jws_token',
         narration='Fourth demo: a compact signed token, J W S. [[slnc 400]] Before signing, two short texts: a header, which says the algorithm is E D D S A, and the payload. [[slnc 500]] Each is written in web-safe base sixty four. [[slnc 300]] The header becomes e y J h b G c i, and so on. [[slnc 300]] The signature is Ed twenty five five one nine, over the header and payload together. [[slnc 500]] After signing, the three parts are joined by dots. [[slnc 400]] An attacker can write a header that says the algorithm is none. [[slnc 300]] A good verifier ignores it, because it always expects E D D S A.'),
    dict(key='17-act-4-1', kind='console', title='Act Four — A compact signed token: JWS',
         body='FOUR. A compact signed token: JWS.\n  BEFORE SIGNING (the RFC 8037 example):\n    header       {"alg":"EdDSA"}\n    payload      Example of Ed25519 signing\n  AFTER SIGNING (each part base64url, joined by dots):\n    header       eyJhbGciOiJFZERTQSJ9\n    payload      RXhhbXBsZSBvZiBFZDI1NTE5IHNpZ25pbmc\n    signature    hgyY0il_MGCjP0JzlnLWG1PPOt7-09PGcvMg3AIbQR6\n                 dWbhijcNR4ki4iylGjg5BhVsPt9g7sVvpAr_MuM0KAg\n    the token in RFC 8037: true; it verifies: true',
         narration='The real output. [[slnc 400]] The header and payload before signing. [[slnc 300]] The three web-safe parts after. [[slnc 300]] Exactly the token in the standard, and it verifies. [[slnc 500]]'),
